    "summary": "In the shell's renderContent (vscode-plugin/src/chat/docs-review-panel.ts), a content for the document already shown is a reload in place: the scrollTop of the document region (#insrc-rv-scroll) is taken before the body is rendered again and put back after, and when the content is marked changed (===true) and its contentVersion differs from the one shown, the result line says 'This document changed on disk and was reloaded.'. The re-read after the shell's own decision is not marked changed, so the decision's result line stays; the watch's later report of that same write carries the version already shown and says nothing. Drafts and the whole-document field are kept by the existing same-document path. Test: the one named test added (the harness models a browser putting the region back at the top when the body is rendered); the shell baseline recomputed with a history line. Pane tests 226/226; whole plugin suite: only the two existing manifest-catalog failures; plugin typecheck clean. Six of seven mutations failed the test; the seventh is equivalent (the value it changes is not used for another document).",
